# EXPECT: binds null to parameter 'b' and the callee reads it
# ouroboros#182: `add of [7]` binds b = null on the VM; add reads b only under
# a guard the VM never fails (prints 7, rc 0), but b's inferred C class is a
# double, which has no null, so the AOT refuses by name instead of leaking
# gcc's "too few arguments" (the pre-#182 behaviour, no AOT: line).
define add(a, b) as:
    if a > 100:
        return a + b
    return a
print of (add of [7])
